    {
      "type": "vis",
      "grid": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 33,
        "w": 48,
        "h": 13
      },
      "config": {
        "type": "data_table",
        "title": "[S3 + Elasticsearch] Toy-train exposure in 2026",
        "data_source": {
          "type": "esql",
          "query": "FROM santa_deliveries_2025\n| WHERE gift_category == \"toy_train\"\n| STATS historical_total = COUNT(*), historical_late = COUNT(*) WHERE delay_minutes > 0 BY gift_category, carrier, country\n| LOOKUP JOIN santa_delivery_plan_2026_v2 ON gift_category, carrier, country\n| EVAL historical_late_rate = 100.0 * historical_late / historical_total, illustrative_late_deliveries = 1.0 * planned_deliveries * historical_late / historical_total\n| EVAL late_rate_gap = historical_late_rate - target_late_rate\n| KEEP carrier, country, historical_total, historical_late, historical_late_rate, planned_deliveries, target_late_rate, late_rate_gap, illustrative_late_deliveries\n| SORT historical_late_rate DESC, carrier ASC, country ASC\n| LIMIT 10\n"
        },
        "rows": [
          {
            "column": "carrier",
            "label": "Carrier"
          },
          {
            "column": "country",
            "label": "Country"
          }
        ],
        "metrics": [
          {
            "column": "historical_total",
            "label": "2025 total",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 0,
              "compact": false
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "historical_late",
            "label": "2025 late",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 0,
              "compact": false
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "historical_late_rate",
            "label": "2025 late (%)",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 1,
              "suffix": "%",
              "compact": false
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "planned_deliveries",
            "label": "2026 planned",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 0,
              "compact": false
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "target_late_rate",
            "label": "Target (%)",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 1,
              "suffix": "%",
              "compact": false
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "late_rate_gap",
            "label": "Gap to target (pp)",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 1,
              "suffix": " pp",
              "compact": false
            },
            "apply_color_to": "background",
            "color": {
              "type": "dynamic",
              "range": "absolute",
              "steps": [
                {
                  "lt": -2,
                  "color": "#2E7D50"
                },
                {
                  "gte": -2,
                  "lt": 5,
                  "color": "#F59E0B"
                },
                {
                  "gte": 5,
                  "color": "#D92D35"
                }
              ]
            }
          },
          {
            "column": "illustrative_late_deliveries",
            "label": "Illustrative late",
            "format": {
              "type": "number",
              "decimals": 1,
              "compact": false
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "grid": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 46,
        "w": 48,
        "h": 6
      },
      "config": {
        "content": "**Interpretation:** `illustrative_late_deliveries = planned_deliveries * historical_late / historical_total`. This applies the 2025 rate to the 2026 plan as an **illustrative unchanged-rate scenario, not a forecast**.\n\nThe 2025 archive remains external; only the 2026 plan is indexed. Data Federation is experimental, and this MinIO compatibility experiment is not officially supported by Elastic.\n\n**Gap colors:** green below \u22122 pp; orange from \u22122 to below +5 pp; red at +5 pp or above. Gap = historical late rate \u2212 route target. Chart colors identify gift categories; table colors indicate the gap to target."
      }
    }
